1
00:00:01,880 --> 00:00:04,420
So, whaddya want from us this time?

2
00:00:04,830 --> 00:00:10,380
Here's the thing. From what I've been told,
the baron will paying us a visit next month.

3
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,500
The baron himself?!

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:15,540
More like the clown who thinks it's cool
to just demand 20 boars from us.

5
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:20,290
He's expressed interest in observing
your boar hunts firsthand.

6
00:00:20,380 --> 00:00:24,380
Great. First he wants more boars, now he wants
a show. Will the surprises never stop?

7
00:00:24,630 --> 00:00:25,920
Well, that's fine with me.

8
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:27,750
But why ask Allen to join us?

9
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:33,500
Let me explain. We need someone to serve
as a tour guide for the baron during his stay.

10
00:00:33,500 --> 00:00:34,040
Huh?

11
00:00:34,540 --> 00:00:35,540
You want me?

12
00:00:35,790 --> 00:00:37,790
Why not just have your own son do it?

13
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,040
My Pelomas isn't suited to the task, I'm afraid.

14
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:42,670
You can say that again.

15
00:00:43,330 --> 00:00:46,630
I'm hoping Allen can help us
show the baron hospitality starting with dinner

16
00:00:46,630 --> 00:00:48,000
the night before the hunt.

17
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:51,210
So, basically, he wants me to entertain
the big cheese while he's in town.

18
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,380
And he's trying to win me over
with these molmo fruits.

19
00:00:53,710 --> 00:00:56,040
Sorry, pal. But I ain't that cheap!

20
00:00:56,460 --> 00:01:01,500
I've heard it was Allen's clever ideas
that led to the success of your hunts last year.

21
00:01:01,630 --> 00:01:03,420
I'm sure he can handle this important job.

22
00:01:03,830 --> 00:01:05,210
What do you say, Allen?

23
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:08,040
Frankly, I couldn't care less about the baron.

24
00:01:08,380 --> 00:01:11,540
But I won't get any chances
to leave the village as a serf.

25
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:16,960
And it'll take 10 years of hunting boars and
albaherons before I can reach commoner status...

26
00:01:18,170 --> 00:01:20,130
You can refuse if you want, okay?

27
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,330
If I remember right, there was one more ticket
to rising the social ladder...

28
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:29,420
The baron can gift people with commoner status.

29
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:30,830
Alright, then.

30
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:35,330
It's okay, Dad. I'll be the baron's tour guide!

31
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:09,920
EPISODE 6: OUTWARD BOUND

32
00:03:16,580 --> 00:03:19,500
Welcome! We're honored
to have you, Baron Granvelle.

33
00:03:19,830 --> 00:03:21,080
Thanks for the warm welcome.

34
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,210
Of course!

35
00:03:22,420 --> 00:03:23,250
Come, Cecil.

36
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:24,330
Okay.

37
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:35,630
Chief Deboji. I appreciate the work that you've
put in over the years to establish Krena Village.

38
00:03:36,170 --> 00:03:39,080
It's been 15 years since
the Land Reclamation Decree.

39
00:03:39,420 --> 00:03:42,920
And there has been no greater success
than here in the Granvelle fiefdom.

40
00:03:43,210 --> 00:03:45,000
Thank you, milord.

41
00:03:45,330 --> 00:03:47,880
Also, I must apologize
for all the fuss over boar meat.

42
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:51,040
I knew asking for more would burden you unduly.

43
00:03:51,250 --> 00:03:54,250
But I simply could not refuse an order
from His Majesty.

44
00:03:54,420 --> 00:03:56,460
F-f-from the King, you say?!

45
00:03:56,630 --> 00:03:58,540
Technically speaking, yes.

46
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:01,380
But the blame truly lies with Viscount Carnel.

47
00:04:01,920 --> 00:04:03,040
That scoundrel!

48
00:04:03,330 --> 00:04:06,210
Calling attention to the boar hunts
while we're in front of the King!

49
00:04:07,460 --> 00:04:10,670
Milord. Your tone is frightening the chieftain.

50
00:04:24,330 --> 00:04:25,960
My God! Exquisite!

51
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:29,540
Father! This meat is quite delicious!

52
00:04:29,880 --> 00:04:32,080
What kind of meat is this, Chief Deboji?

53
00:04:32,290 --> 00:04:34,960
Huh? Oh, um, well...

54
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:37,960
If I may interrupt, this is a dish of albaheron.

55
00:04:38,420 --> 00:04:40,420
The meat is from one hunted just yesterday.

56
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:43,080
Only the freshest ingredients for you, milord.

57
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:48,170
It uses the breast meat, thigh meat,
and liver, all flavored with a blend of herbs.

58
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,420
Ah, I see.

59
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,420
Is this your son, Chief Deboji?

60
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:55,210
No, actually. This is the son of Rodin, one of...

61
00:04:55,210 --> 00:04:57,710
Oh! Rodin the Boar Hunter's son, eh?

62
00:04:58,040 --> 00:05:00,790
Now I remember why your black hair
and eyes seem familiar.

63
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:04,080
It's good to see you again, Sir Zenof.

64
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:07,330
I will be serving as your guide
during tomorrow's hunt.

65
00:05:07,670 --> 00:05:09,670
Such a well-mannered young man.

66
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:12,580
Is his father a former member of the knighthood?

67
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:15,460
No, milord. He comes from a family of serfs.

68
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:18,380
Serfs?! You let one of them into your guest hall?!

69
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:22,080
Cecil! You know that serfs
are fair members of our fiefdom.

70
00:05:22,210 --> 00:05:24,170
Don't treat them like some kind of animal.

71
00:05:24,290 --> 00:05:26,830
Right. I'm very sorry, Father.

72
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,420
Why do I get the stink eye?

73
00:05:31,830 --> 00:05:33,210
Son of Rodin.

74
00:05:33,670 --> 00:05:37,250
I hope you're ready to acquaint us
on the finer details during tomorrow's hunt.

75
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:38,960
Yes. Of course, sir.

76
00:05:39,250 --> 00:05:41,830
Wrangling 20 boars in one year is a steep goal.

77
00:05:42,250 --> 00:05:46,630
Should it prove too difficult,
then my knights will take over the hunts.

78
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:47,790
Uh-huh.

79
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,670
Not convinced we serfs have what it takes, are ya?

80
00:05:51,290 --> 00:05:53,250
That would be most wonderful, Zenof!

81
00:05:53,500 --> 00:05:57,330
I asked my father to let me tag along
because I wanted to see a great boar up close,

82
00:05:57,630 --> 00:06:00,500
but seeing the knights slay
one would be even better!

83
00:06:01,290 --> 00:06:01,920
Sure.

84
00:06:02,380 --> 00:06:03,960
Once you've shown them the fundamentals,

85
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:06,210
the knights can handle
the responsibility of hunting.

86
00:06:06,290 --> 00:06:09,710
I beg your pardon, milord.
But 20 boars is a paltry number.

87
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:11,000
Huh?!

88
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:14,290
We will have no problems meeting the quota.

89
00:06:14,670 --> 00:06:16,670
Our performance tomorrow
should convince you of that.

90
00:06:23,420 --> 00:06:27,920
Zenof. I'm leaving Cecil under your protection.
I expect you to keep her safe.

91
00:06:28,130 --> 00:06:30,290
Of course, my lord. It shall be done.

92
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:41,460
This is so exciting, Sebas!

93
00:06:41,460 --> 00:06:43,170
Indeed, milady.

94
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:54,540
Here we are. You'll be able to see
all of today's action from atop this watchtower.

95
00:06:55,040 --> 00:06:56,330
Please head on up.

96
00:06:56,790 --> 00:06:57,460
Hmph!

97
00:07:02,750 --> 00:07:05,040
Wow, what a great view!

98
00:07:05,040 --> 00:07:07,540
Indeed. Trees as far as the eye can see.

99
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:10,540
This is the forest where the great boars nest.

100
00:07:13,790 --> 00:07:14,920
The hunters have arrived.

101
00:07:15,130 --> 00:07:17,920
Ah, I see they've got armor!

102
00:07:18,330 --> 00:07:20,710
We made good use of the boars from last year.

103
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:23,580
That armor was forged
from leftover pelts, bones, and fangs.

104
00:07:23,960 --> 00:07:26,710
I was asked to thank you
for granting permission, milord.

105
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:29,750
On behalf of my father, Rodin.

106
00:07:30,960 --> 00:07:32,170
Okay, let's move out!

107
00:07:33,130 --> 00:07:33,960
What are they doing?

108
00:07:34,460 --> 00:07:37,170
Their job is to lure boars
into the hunting grounds.

109
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,830
Speed is a key factor,
so they are only lightly equipped.

110
00:07:40,170 --> 00:07:41,290
Huh.

111
00:07:41,630 --> 00:07:47,040
Please be patient as it may take time to lure
the boars, despite how many live in the forest.

112
00:07:47,290 --> 00:07:48,000
Fair enough.

113
00:07:48,630 --> 00:07:50,040
That reminds me, Allen.

114
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,380
How is the Sword Lord, Krena, fairing these days?

115
00:07:53,580 --> 00:07:55,380
Ah, she's doing great!

116
00:07:55,710 --> 00:07:56,830
Wonderful.

117
00:07:57,000 --> 00:07:59,750
Let her know a tutor will be dispatched
here the spring after next to help her study

118
00:07:59,750 --> 00:08:01,830
for the Academy entrance exam.

119
00:08:02,080 --> 00:08:03,210
Understood.

120
00:08:03,630 --> 00:08:06,880
It's hard to imagine Krena studying for anything.

121
00:08:07,170 --> 00:08:08,420
She's gonna look so silly!

122
00:08:10,830 --> 00:08:11,790
Here comes the first one!

123
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:14,790
Heads up!

124
00:08:20,290 --> 00:08:22,000
Heave-ho!

125
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,080
As you can see, we start by boxing them in.

126
00:08:25,630 --> 00:08:27,880
Those large shields are made from two layers

127
00:08:27,880 --> 00:08:30,540
of the toughest part of the boar hide,
found on its back.

128
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:31,880
Strike team, you're up!

129
00:08:35,540 --> 00:08:36,540
Long spear team!

130
00:08:37,130 --> 00:08:40,580
The long spear team consists of the least
experienced members, who just joined last year.

131
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:44,500
The frontliners with the toughest job
are the ones wearing armor, I see.

132
00:08:44,670 --> 00:08:49,830
Yes. It also covers their backs to prevent injury
if one of the long spear team misses the target.

133
00:08:50,960 --> 00:08:52,380
The boar's neck is the best place to strike.

134
00:08:57,330 --> 00:08:58,830
That was a fatal blow.

135
00:08:58,830 --> 00:09:01,040
Ugh...

136
00:09:05,750 --> 00:09:07,170
Wow. Most impressive.

137
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:09,750
Milady! Milady!

138
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:13,040
These men may not be knights, Your Lordship,

139
00:09:13,040 --> 00:09:16,460
but I believe they are worthy
of being called warriors.

140
00:09:16,750 --> 00:09:19,500
Yes, I must applaud their fighting prowess.

141
00:09:19,830 --> 00:09:21,460
It seems there will be no problem with-

142
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,130
Incoming!

143
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:27,630
Two boars at once?!

144
00:09:27,920 --> 00:09:29,790
Leibrand, make ready to assist!

145
00:09:29,790 --> 00:09:30,210
Yessir!

146
00:09:30,210 --> 00:09:31,080
Please wait.

147
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:33,080
There is no need to panic.

148
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:35,710
The hunting team is trained to deal
with these situations.

149
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:36,540
But even so!

150
00:09:36,750 --> 00:09:38,380
Please let them handle it.

151
00:09:39,130 --> 00:09:40,960
Stick to your training and split into two groups!

152
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:44,000
Gerda and I will take the lead! Move out!

153
00:09:46,790 --> 00:09:50,540
Every hunter worth their salt
knows to kill all the game they bait.

154
00:09:51,210 --> 00:09:52,670
Letting anything escape is folly.

155
00:09:53,670 --> 00:09:57,380
But for the past 10 years, my dad
and the other serfs haven't been able to do that.

156
00:09:57,880 --> 00:10:00,290
Mainly due to their lack of armor.

157
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:04,710
Sixty percent of their hard-earned
boar meat gets taken as tax.

158
00:10:05,210 --> 00:10:07,880
And they have to exchange
the rest for daily necessities.

159
00:10:08,540 --> 00:10:11,040
Spears were the only thing
they could afford to upgrade.

160
00:10:11,540 --> 00:10:14,170
However, it's possible for them
to create some leeway by mastering

161
00:10:14,170 --> 00:10:15,670
the most efficient hunting strategy.

162
00:10:16,040 --> 00:10:20,000
That allows for gradual equipment upgrades,
which then raises their efficiency even higher.

163
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,000
It's the most basic of basics!

164
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:27,540
Milady!

165
00:10:31,880 --> 00:10:33,170
Not again!

166
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:37,210
That's three boars down. All's going well!

167
00:10:37,710 --> 00:10:42,130
Thank God. Watching them fight two at once
still has me sweating bullets.

168
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:44,460
That leaves 17 more to go.

169
00:10:44,670 --> 00:10:46,210
No, milord. Just 10, actually.

170
00:10:46,540 --> 00:10:47,630
Really?!

171
00:10:47,960 --> 00:10:51,380
Seven boars had already been hunted this year
before you graced us with your presence.

172
00:10:51,710 --> 00:10:54,920
I imagine we'll have filled the quota
by this time next month!

173
00:10:55,380 --> 00:10:57,040
You don't say!

174
00:10:57,380 --> 00:11:00,330
Doesn't seem like my knights
will be needed, after all.

175
00:11:00,670 --> 00:11:03,630
Thank you. My father and the others
will be happy to hear it.

176
00:11:04,580 --> 00:11:08,080
If I may, we actually have two requests
to make of you, milord.

177
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,080
Is that so? What are they?

178
00:11:10,670 --> 00:11:15,210
For starters, we humbly ask for permission
to make two more of the shield walls.

179
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:18,000
In the interest of hunting
even more next year, I assume?

180
00:11:18,210 --> 00:11:18,790
Exactly.

181
00:11:19,210 --> 00:11:20,830
Very well. What else?

182
00:11:21,080 --> 00:11:24,580
Secondly, we want to procure goods
not available in the village.

183
00:11:24,830 --> 00:11:27,580
Specifically... liquor.

184
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:28,880
Liquor?

185
00:11:29,330 --> 00:11:33,580
We would like your permission to trade in liquor
and allow its distribution among the serfs.

186
00:11:34,130 --> 00:11:35,420
But what for?

187
00:11:36,210 --> 00:11:38,540
As more and more boars are hunted,

188
00:11:38,790 --> 00:11:40,750
there is a real concern that the
resulting abundance of meat

189
00:11:40,750 --> 00:11:42,540
will reduce its value in the village.

190
00:11:43,170 --> 00:11:47,380
Exchanging the meat for imported liquor
instead will help to prevent a market crash.

191
00:11:48,080 --> 00:11:49,540
Why liquor specifically?

192
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:53,540
Given his position, this something
that Sir Zenof may understand better, but...

193
00:11:53,880 --> 00:11:56,330
the hunters must risk their lives to be effective.

194
00:11:57,170 --> 00:12:01,330
I get it. You need the liquor
to help keep their morale high, yes?

195
00:12:01,330 --> 00:12:02,460
Precisely.

196
00:12:02,960 --> 00:12:05,040
That's how my father explained it to me.

197
00:12:05,540 --> 00:12:10,790
Your Lordship. I am of the mind
that their request stands to very good reason.

198
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,630
Then I shall consider it favorably.

199
00:12:14,250 --> 00:12:15,580
Allen, was it?

200
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,040
I must say, you have done a splendid job today.

201
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,250
Thank you, milord.

202
00:12:23,290 --> 00:12:24,670
Hey, you!

203
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:29,380
You were lucky to get any praise from my father!
Don't let it go to your head!

204
00:12:29,460 --> 00:12:31,210
I mean, you barely even...

205
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:33,630
Careful, milady!

206
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:36,960
Hmph!

207
00:12:37,540 --> 00:12:39,670
Let us be on our way, milady.

208
00:12:40,420 --> 00:12:43,210
Yeesh. Talk about a delicate damsel.

209
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,670
Go back to your cushy city life.

210
00:12:46,170 --> 00:12:47,880
That's probably the last I see of her.

211
00:12:52,710 --> 00:12:54,330
Rodin. Gerda.

212
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:55,210
Yessir!

213
00:12:55,580 --> 00:12:57,630
You've truly shown me what you're capable of.

214
00:12:57,880 --> 00:12:59,920
I must commend your amazing hunting skills.

215
00:13:02,420 --> 00:13:06,290
Your accomplishments deserve to be rewarded.
I wouldn't make a good baron otherwise.

216
00:13:07,540 --> 00:13:09,580
Aw, yeah! Now you're talking!

217
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:13,380
Don't bother with money!
We want social mobility, baby! Come on commoner!

218
00:13:14,080 --> 00:13:20,460
Rodin. Gerda. I hereby elevate you
and your families... to commoner status!

219
00:13:23,330 --> 00:13:26,330
I expect that you'll continue to work hard.

220
00:13:26,580 --> 00:13:28,880
Yessir! Thank you very much!

221
00:13:29,130 --> 00:13:30,380
Thank you, milord!

222
00:13:30,380 --> 00:13:31,960
HELL YES!

223
00:13:32,130 --> 00:13:34,460
Goodbye serfdom! Hello commoner status!

224
00:13:34,540 --> 00:13:36,960
Now I can go hunting outside the village limits!

225
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:39,960
I've dreamed about this moment
countless times over the past eight years!

226
00:13:40,250 --> 00:13:43,170
My first stop: the White Dragon Mountains
to go dragon hunting!

227
00:13:45,170 --> 00:13:48,540
For any serfs who have taken part
in the hunts for over 10 years,

228
00:13:48,630 --> 00:13:50,330
I shall also grant the same status.

229
00:13:50,710 --> 00:13:54,080
Do a thorough check and determine
who among your team are eligible.

230
00:13:54,380 --> 00:13:54,880
Yessir!

231
00:13:55,290 --> 00:13:57,500
I foresee no problems
fulfilling His Majesty's order.

232
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,380
Now I can return to the city and rest easy.

233
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:01,830
Milord.

234
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:02,710
What is it?

235
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,960
I believe there was one more thing
His Majesty was keen to know.

236
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,710
Ah! I nearly forgot!

237
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:13,380
His Majesty wishes to promote Krena Village
as a shining example for the rest of the kingdom.

238
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:16,540
Thus, he asked me for the details
of how the boar hunts began.

239
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:19,290
Y-you want to know the history behind it?

240
00:14:19,290 --> 00:14:21,250
I haven't heard that story, myself.

241
00:14:21,460 --> 00:14:25,080
That's actually a sore subject
for Rodin, Your Lordship.

242
00:14:25,460 --> 00:14:27,630
May I tell it in his stead?

243
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:29,250
By all means.

244
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:35,790
It all started in spring... 13 years ago...

245
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,000
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

246
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:41,000
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

247
00:14:42,670 --> 00:14:45,380
About 100 serfs from nearby villages
relocated here to help develop the land

248
00:14:45,920 --> 00:14:48,540
as part of the Reclamation Decree.

249
00:14:49,420 --> 00:14:52,040
After six months of hard work,
we had cleared out a good chunk of the forest.

250
00:14:52,670 --> 00:14:55,880
Fall was on the horizon when disaster struck.

251
00:14:57,330 --> 00:14:59,380
A great boar came out of nowhere and attacked us,

252
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:04,000
devouring most of the wheat and potatoes
that we had set aside for winter.

253
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:07,920
The majority of serfs had chosen
to brave the frontier

254
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:09,580
after struggling to obtain food
in their old villages.

255
00:15:10,080 --> 00:15:11,960
Which meant going back wasn't an option.

256
00:15:13,330 --> 00:15:15,040
That's when Rodin spoke up.

257
00:15:15,630 --> 00:15:17,880
He proposed we hunt the boars for meat.

258
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:22,290
Back then, we didn't have any of the weapons,
armor, or knowledge that we do now.

259
00:15:22,920 --> 00:15:26,250
In spite of that, all the men united to go hunting
with pickaxes and hoes as weapons,

260
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:29,080
and we managed to kill a single boar.

261
00:15:31,710 --> 00:15:33,790
That sounds like a story to pride yourself on.

262
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,330
You came together to accomplish a difficult task.

263
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:40,420
The problem is... we lost a friend in the process.

264
00:15:41,630 --> 00:15:46,790
After defeating the boar, we overcame
a Trial of the Gods and our injuries were healed.

265
00:15:47,420 --> 00:15:50,250
But our friend wasn't as fortunate.

266
00:15:51,080 --> 00:15:53,540
I've told Rodin over and over again
that he shouldn't blame himself,

267
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,790
but he just won't hear it.

268
00:15:56,750 --> 00:15:57,750
So that's it.

269
00:15:58,170 --> 00:16:00,330
Now I understand why Dad
covered for that commoner.

270
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:03,580
It's because he once lost a friend the same way.

271
00:16:05,250 --> 00:16:09,250
Hrm. I'm sorry to dredge up such a painful memory.

272
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,080
That's okay.

273
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:14,500
But listen, Rodin. Although lives were lost,
the village could never have come this far

274
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:16,130
without your prudent actions.

275
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:20,000
Let me honor the bravery of your youth
with one more reward.

276
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:21,580
Ask of me whatever you wish.

277
00:16:21,790 --> 00:16:22,460
Huh?!

278
00:16:23,080 --> 00:16:25,960
Oh, sweet! That triggered a bonus event!

279
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:28,460
A nice cherry on top before we wrap this up!

280
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:31,210
Congratulations, Dad! Ask him for some liquor!

281
00:16:32,130 --> 00:16:35,460
Well, Baron Granvelle... I do have one request.

282
00:16:36,290 --> 00:16:40,040
Would you please allow my son
to work at your estate?

283
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:41,130
Huh?!

284
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:44,380
Allen has a better head
on his shoulders than I do.

285
00:16:44,750 --> 00:16:46,460
Any job is fine, even just hallboy.

286
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:48,130
I promise that he'll be an asset!

287
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:49,420
Huh? Wait.

288
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:51,250
No! Bad idea, Dad!

289
00:16:51,250 --> 00:16:54,380
That is not what I had in mind!
It... it could ruin everything!

290
00:16:54,540 --> 00:16:57,210
Hmm. Work at my estate, eh?

291
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,710
Sebas?

292
00:16:59,170 --> 00:17:03,670
I have no problems with it.
He seems plenty clever to me.

293
00:17:03,880 --> 00:17:05,580
Say no, dammit!

294
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:07,710
Let me live my dream of hunting legendary dragons!

295
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:10,420
I'll have even LESS freedom living with the baron!

296
00:17:10,540 --> 00:17:13,830
G-g-g-gotta think. Must be a way outta this.

297
00:17:14,790 --> 00:17:17,500
A hallboy, eh? No, that won't do.

298
00:17:17,710 --> 00:17:20,250
Crap, crap, crap. Please don't...

299
00:17:18,670 --> 00:17:20,250
Allen, son of Rodin.

300
00:17:21,460 --> 00:17:25,630
I hereby appoint you...
as manservant of the Granvelle Family.

301
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,170
WHAT?!

302
00:17:27,250 --> 00:17:29,920
M-manservant?! Really, milord?!

303
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:32,420
You can't be serious, Father!

304
00:17:32,540 --> 00:17:35,580
Just the idea of having a serf
in our house makes me sick!

305
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:37,670
He is a commoner now, milady.

306
00:17:39,960 --> 00:17:42,880
How are hallboy and manservant any different?!

307
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:45,460
Wait, forget that!
I need to get myself out of this mess!

308
00:17:45,460 --> 00:17:47,830
Think! Come up with some excuse!

309
00:17:48,210 --> 00:17:48,790
Allen!

310
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:00,040
I look forward to serving you, milord...

311
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:04,210
Damn. There's just no way I can turn it down.

312
00:18:04,960 --> 00:18:05,920
I'm boned.

313
00:18:12,130 --> 00:18:14,290
All set. It looks great on you, Allen.

314
00:18:14,420 --> 00:18:15,960
Thanks, Mom.

315
00:18:31,630 --> 00:18:33,710
Aw, Allen. You really gotta go?

316
00:18:34,380 --> 00:18:36,880
Yeah. Take care of yourself, Krena.

317
00:18:38,580 --> 00:18:40,830
Hey, Krena. How about one more duel before I go?

318
00:18:41,130 --> 00:18:41,880
Yay!

319
00:18:42,330 --> 00:18:46,380
I am Krena the Fierce! Have at thee!

320
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:50,330
I am Allen, manservant to Baron Granvelle!

321
00:18:52,290 --> 00:18:54,630
Sword Lord Krena! Do your worst!

322
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:56,330
Here I come!

323
00:18:59,330 --> 00:19:01,130
What a good way for them to say goodbye.

324
00:19:01,330 --> 00:19:02,330
That's for sure.

325
00:19:02,790 --> 00:19:03,920
Tugs at the heartstrings.

326
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,790
What's going on?

327
00:19:08,330 --> 00:19:10,460
Whoa, is Allen... overpowering Krena?!

328
00:19:11,080 --> 00:19:15,330
I used nearly all the magic stones that I
had stocked up and created 20 copies of Hawkins.

329
00:19:15,580 --> 00:19:17,960
I went all in on agility!

330
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:22,420
When Krena turns 12,
she'll leave to study in Academy City.

331
00:19:22,580 --> 00:19:24,830
Then she'll go into the royal service.

332
00:19:25,540 --> 00:19:27,540
It's possible we'll never see each other again.

333
00:19:32,210 --> 00:19:34,000
Did I just lose...?

334
00:19:34,830 --> 00:19:36,130
Sword Lord Krena.

335
00:19:37,130 --> 00:19:39,380
I think we can both agree that this was a draw.

336
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,750
It was?

337
00:19:42,290 --> 00:19:45,790
We'll settle this in the future,
when we meet again!

338
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:50,420
Okay! I'm gonna win for sure, Allen!

339
00:19:52,790 --> 00:19:54,750
Now there's the smile I wanted to see.

340
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,670
Allen.

341
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,540
Take care not to get sick, okay?

342
00:19:59,880 --> 00:20:00,500
Okay.

343
00:20:02,920 --> 00:20:04,330
No more tears, Mash.

344
00:20:04,420 --> 00:20:07,210
You have to step up to protect Mom and Myulla now!

345
00:20:09,630 --> 00:20:11,170
Hey. Say goodbye to Myulla, too.

346
00:20:11,500 --> 00:20:14,500
Myulla. Grow up nice and big, okay?

347
00:20:15,710 --> 00:20:20,540
I still remember helping deliver you
as a baby, kiddo. It makes me sad to see you go.

348
00:20:20,880 --> 00:20:23,330
Shucks, Miss Mathilda. Thank you.

349
00:20:23,580 --> 00:20:25,420
Stay safe, Allen.

350
00:20:25,630 --> 00:20:26,290
I will.

351
00:20:26,630 --> 00:20:28,380
Thanks for everything!

352
00:20:29,080 --> 00:20:30,380
Hey, don't push me.

353
00:20:31,170 --> 00:20:32,130
Aw, crap!

354
00:20:34,830 --> 00:20:35,750
Dogora?

355
00:20:36,580 --> 00:20:37,460
And Pelomas?

356
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:39,750
Uh, hi.

357
00:20:41,710 --> 00:20:42,290
Here.

358
00:20:42,750 --> 00:20:43,960
It's for me?

359
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:49,670
Hmph! Don't say I never gave you nothin'!

360
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:56,250
That kid's a riot!

361
00:20:56,380 --> 00:20:57,830
And generous to boot!

362
00:20:58,330 --> 00:20:58,920
Yeah!

363
00:21:00,210 --> 00:21:01,420
Let's get going, Allen.

364
00:21:01,830 --> 00:21:02,460
Right.

365
00:21:17,790 --> 00:21:18,460
Allen.

366
00:21:19,130 --> 00:21:21,380
Manservant is only the first step for you.

367
00:21:22,040 --> 00:21:23,880
Work hard and you'll go places.

368
00:21:24,330 --> 00:21:26,330
Yeah. I'll do my best!

369
00:21:33,670 --> 00:21:36,460
Hey! They're almost ready to leave!

370
00:21:36,670 --> 00:21:38,210
Bye, son. Make me proud.

371
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:42,210
Come home if it gets too tough, okay?

372
00:22:23,630 --> 00:22:24,960
Goodbye, everybody.

